  "name": "Lovecraft Country",
  "description": "The fog-bound coast and backcountry of 1920s Massachusetts that H.P. Lovecraft wrote as the epicenter of the Cthulhu Mythos — witch-haunted Arkham and Miskatonic University, the decaying fishing town of Innsmouth, the blighted hill country around Dunwich, and the ancient seaport of Kingsport. Investigators here are ordinary people — professors, journalists, private eyes, doctors — pulled into cosmic horrors far beyond human understanding.",
